  "chapter": 344,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 48 Chapter 344\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8782, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the election law, in relation to requiring munici-\n        palities with the highest population in each county to  have  at\n        least one polling place designated for early voting\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  amends the Election Law to require every municipality with\nthe highest population in each county to have at least one polling place\ndesignated for early voting. To the  extent  practicable,  such  polling\nplaces  shall  be  situated  near public transportation. The legislation\nfurther increases the ceiling for early voting polling places from seven\nto ten.\n \n  This bill will increase access to early voting across New York. As the\nrecent presidential election shows, access to early voting  is  critical\nto  ensuring  that  New  Yorkers  have options when casting their ballot\nduring an election. By requiring municipalities with the  highest  popu-\nlations  to  have  an early voting site, we are ensuring more convenient\naccess for all New Yorkers.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to fix one  technical\nissue  with  the  legislation's requirements in Washington County. While\nFort Edward is the County Seat, nearby Hudson Falls  is  the  population\ncenter.  The  two  municipalities are separated by about three miles and\nhave a population difference of approximately  one  thousand  residents.\nRequiring  multiple  early  voting  sites  to be in such close proximity\nwould create an operational burden for the Washington  County  Board  of\nElections  while  providing  little  benefit  to voters. The legislation\nensures that Washington County will be in compliance  with  the  law  so\nlong  as  it  maintains  one  early voting site in either the population\ncenter or County Seat. On the basis of this agreement, I am  pleased  to\nsign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
